            <ArticleTitle>[Spontaneous hemoperitoneum during pregnancy and uterine artery aneurysm].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>711-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.gyobfe.2012.07.006</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1297-9589(12)00195-6</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Spontaneous hemoperitoneum is not frequent. We report here a rare cause of spontaneous hemoperitoneum during the second trimester of pregnancy. A ruptured uterine artery aneurysm was revealed in a patient who came for important abdominal pain. A CT scan showed a large hemoperitoneum and an additional arterial image. The patient underwent rapidly an embolization, which allowed a complete closure of the aneurysm. The patient gave birth to a healthy child. The diagnosis of hemoperitoneum must be discussed without delay. Once imagery realised, a good management of the patient must be done depending on the origin of the hemoperitoneum.</AbstractText>
